 ## Background
-VoxelGrid was introduced as a key component in Differentiable Volumetric Graphics (DVGO), a method proposed as a faster alternative to the original Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) which used a fully connected MLP [S1, unofficial]. By storing density and color in a voxel grid and using differentiable trilinear interpolation, DVGO enabled efficient training and rendering of neural radiance fields [S1, unofficial]. This approach is widely used in modern neural rendering pipelines for its balance of speed and quality.
